diagnostics/language-habits.em:2:14: this is Int, but `remove` needs String
  names.remove(0)
               ^
`remove` takes the item itself, not its position. To remove the item at a position, write `names.remove_at(0)`.
diagnostics/language-habits.em:5:5: `break` can only be used inside a loop
      break if n > 1
      ^^^^^
`break` ends a `for` or `while` loop; a block passed to `each` or `map` is not a loop. Write a `for` loop over the items instead, as in `for item in items`.
diagnostics/language-habits.em:11:7: only an Error can be raised, but this is BadScore
  raise BadScore("too high")
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Only an `Error` can be raised. Declare it as `class BadScore extends Error`, so it can be raised and caught.
